## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical detection pipeline for cloud-native DNS tunneling, combining kernel telemetry, DNS-layer analytics, and service-mesh visibility; emphasizes real-world validation and false-positive control.

## Key Concepts
- eBPF DNS egress monitoring
- CoreDNS analytics and entropy-based signals
- Istio telemetry integration and namespace scoping
- Multi-signal alerting and validation
- Synthetic traffic to verify detections

## Code Example
```javascript
function entropy(s){
  const counts = {};
  for(const ch of s) counts[ch]=(counts[ch]||0)+1;
  const total = s.length;
  let e=0; for(const c of Object.values(counts)){ const p=c/total; e -= p*Math.log2(p); }
  return e;
}
function isSuspicious(domain){
  const parts = domain.split('.');
  const labels = parts.slice(0,-1);
  const ent = labels.map(l=>entropy(l)).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  const len = domain.length;
  return ent>3.5 || len>30;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tune thresholds to reduce false positives across tenants?
- What data retention and RBAC would you implement for CoreDNS and eBPF telemetry?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-cloud IaC security policy gates using industry-standard tools (tfsec, Checkov); covers secret management, encryption, versioning, provider pinning, tagging, and backend security.

## Key Concepts
- Secrets in code and tfvars detection
- Cloud storage encryption and versioning
- Provider version pinning and backends
- Tagging and access controls across clouds
- CI integration and local verification for IaC gates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Failing: plaintext secret in Terraform
variable \"db_password\" { default = \"SuperSecret123\" }
resource \"aws_db_instance\" \"db\" {
  password = var.db_password
}

// Passing: secret retrieved from Secrets Manager
data \"aws_secretsmanager_secret_version\" \"db_pass\" {
  secret_id = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:region:acct:secret:db-password\"
}
resource \"aws_db_instance\" \"db\" {
  password = data.aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.db_pass.secret_string
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you unit-test this gate locally? 
- How would you evolve checks for multi-cloud secret fetch patterns?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluate hands-on ability to translate policy into Gatekeeper and Kyverno, using SPIFFE for workload identity and enforcing data-scoping in a real multi-tenant setup.

## Key Concepts
- Gatekeeper ConstraintTemplate and Constraint
- Kyverno policy enforcement
- SPIFFE IDs for notebook workloads
- Data catalog whitelisting and kernel/runtime controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-check illustrating the policy guard
function isCompliant(pod) {
  const spiffe = pod?.metadata?.annotations?.['spiffe.io/id'];
  const mounts = (pod?.spec?.containers?.[0]?.volumeMounts || [])
    .map(m => m.mountPath);
  const hasWhitelistedData = mounts.some(p => p.startsWith('/data/whitelist'));
  const hasApprovedKernel = !!spiffe && spiffe.startsWith('spiffe://')
    && (pod?.spec?.containers?.[0]?.image || '').includes('approved-runtime');
  return hasWhitelistedData && hasApprovedKernel;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate policy effectiveness in CI/CD and in prod?
- How would you handle exceptions for legitimate data-science projects without widening risk?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical end-to-end security for data integration pipelines, including artifact signing, attestation storage, and runtime enforcement with policy engines.

## Key Concepts

- Artifact signing with cosign and key management
- Attestations stored in Rekor registry
- Policy-driven runtime enforcement (Kyverno/OPA)
- Integration points with Kafka Connect

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal illustration: pseudo-check attestation reference in manifest
async function isAttested(manifest) {
  const ref = manifest.attestationRef;
  // fetch and verify against Rekor/public cosign key
  return !!ref;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle rotation of signing keys and revocation?
- What metrics and alerts would you add to detect failed attestations at startup?
